<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Telkom deal to boost to S.African reserves, rand.</title>
<headline>Telkom deal to boost to S.African reserves, rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The sale of 30 percent of state telecommunications concern Telkom for $1.261 billion will lift foreign exchange reserves and should help the rand, forex dealers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal is the largest foreign direct investment in South Africa to date and will provide a major boost to the country's foreign exchange reserves, currently standing at around $2.8 billion.</p>
<p>SBC Communications Inc and Telekom Malaysia Bhd will make a one-off payment in dollars at the close of the deal, which could be one week to 90 days from Wednesday's signing, officials said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
